  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q01",
      "source_numbers": ["278"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "等比数列 $(x_n)$ 的首项为 $x_1$，公比为 $q$。以下哪一组公式依次表示 $x_5,x_{21},x_{150},x_m,x_{m+2},x_{2k+1}$？各下标均为有效项序号。",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$(x_1q^5,\\ x_1q^{21},\\ x_1q^{150},\\ x_1q^m,\\ x_1q^{m+2},\\ x_1q^{2k+1})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$(x_1q^4,\\ x_1q^{20},\\ x_1q^{149},\\ x_1q^{m-1},\\ x_1q^{m+1},\\ x_1q^{2k})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$(x_1q^8,\\ x_1q^{40},\\ x_1q^{298},\\ x_1q^{2m-2},\\ x_1q^{2m+2},\\ x_1q^{4k})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$(x_1+4q,\\ x_1+20q,\\ x_1+149q,\\ x_1+(m-1)q,\\ x_1+(m+1)q,\\ x_1+2kq)$", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Determine the complete six-term symbolic tuple, including algebraic subscripts.",
        "source_solution": "From the first to the jth term there are j-1 successive multiplications by q. Substituting j=5,21,150,m,m+2,2k+1 into x_j=x_1 q^(j-1) gives respectively x_1 q^4, x_1 q^20, x_1 q^149, x_1 q^(m-1), x_1 q^(m+1), x_1 q^(2k).",
        "unit_reason": "One coherent index-to-exponent rule governs all six coordinates; a whole tuple retains its numerical and symbolic boundary distinctions without six isolated clicks.",
        "concept_blocks": [1],
        "limitations": ["Recognition does not demonstrate unaided production of all six formulas."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["b"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Applying the erroneous formula x_j=x_1q^j to j=5,21,150,m,m+2,2k+1 yields exactly this tuple; it uses one extra multiplication in every coordinate.", "misconception": "Treat the term index itself as the count of ratio multiplications from the first term."},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "The required counts are 4,20,149,m-1,m+1,2k, so substitution into x_j=x_1q^(j-1) gives this entire tuple.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Replace each ratio step q by q^2, giving x_j=x_1q^(2(j-1)); doubling the six correct exponents produces 8,40,298,2m-2,2m+2,4k.", "misconception": "Count two ratio factors instead of one at every adjacent transition."},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The arithmetic-sequence rule x_j=x_1+(j-1)q yields the six displayed sums. For x_1=1,q=2 the fifth term would be 9 rather than 16.", "misconception": "Use the common ratio as an additive common difference."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q02",
      "source_numbers": ["279"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "等比数列 $(u_n)$ 中，$u_1=256$，$q=\\frac12$。以下哪一组依次给出 $u_3,u_5,u_{10},u_n$？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$(32,\\ 8,\\ \\frac14,\\ 256(\\frac12)^n)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$(128,\\ 32,\\ 1,\\ 256(\\frac12)^{n-2})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$(1024,\\ 4096,\\ 131072,\\ 256\\cdot2^{n-1})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$(64,\\ 16,\\ \\frac12,\\ 256(\\frac12)^{n-1})$", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Find three numerical terms and the consistent general formula in one reciprocal-ratio sequence.",
        "source_solution": "u_n=256(1/2)^(n-1)=2^(9-n). Thus u_3=256/4=64, u_5=256/16=16, u_10=256/512=1/2. The general formula returns 256 at n=1.",
        "unit_reason": "The three values are evaluations of the same general formula; combining them preserves consistency, including crossing below 1.",
        "concept_blocks": [1],
        "limitations": ["Recognition replaces independent writing and evaluation of the four results."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["d"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Using 256(1/2)^j instead of exponent j-1 gives 256/8=32,256/32=8,256/1024=1/4 and the displayed general formula.", "misconception": "Make one additional halving before each indexed term."},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Using exponent j-2 gives 256/2=128,256/8=32,256/256=1 and the displayed formula.", "misconception": "Omit one required halving from each index count."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Replacing the ratio 1/2 by its reciprocal 2 yields 256*2^2=1024,256*2^4=4096,256*2^9=131072.", "misconception": "Invert the ratio, so a halving sequence becomes a doubling sequence."},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Exponents 2,4,9 yield 64,16,1/2, and the formula at n=1 gives 256.", "misconception": null}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q03",
      "source_numbers": ["280"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "四个等比数列的首项、公比、所求项序号分别为：\n\n| 数列 | 首项 | 公比 | 项序号 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A | $96$ | $\\frac12$ | $7$ |\n| B | $0.125$ | $-2$ | $6$ |\n| C | $4\\sqrt2$ | $-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}$ | $9$ |\n| D | $0.003$ | $\\sqrt{10}$ | $7$ |\n\n按 A、B、C、D 的顺序，所求项组成哪一组？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$(\\frac32,\\ -4,\\ \\frac{\\sqrt2}{4},\\ 3)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$(\\frac34,\\ 8,\\ -\\frac14,\\ 3\\sqrt{10})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$(\\frac32,\\ 4,\\ \\frac{\\sqrt2}{4},\\ 3)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$(3,\\ -2,\\ -\\frac12,\\ 0.3\\sqrt{10})$", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Evaluate a full four-case tuple across reciprocal, signed, radical and decimal ratios.",
        "source_solution": "a: 96(1/2)^6=96/64=3/2. b: 0.125(-2)^5=(1/8)(-32)=-4. c: 4sqrt(2)(-1/sqrt(2))^8=4sqrt(2)/16=sqrt(2)/4; even exponent removes the negative sign. d: 0.003(sqrt(10))^6=0.003*10^3=3.",
        "unit_reason": "The shared general-term operation is tested across four materially different powers. The tuple retains odd/even sign and radical-decimal distinctions without an item per blank.",
        "concept_blocks": [1],
        "limitations": ["Selection does not demonstrate independent written computation of each power."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["a"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "The four exponents n-1 are 6,5,8,6; direct exact evaluation yields 3/2,-4,sqrt(2)/4,3.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Using n instead of n-1 gives 96/128=3/4,(1/8)*64=8,4sqrt(2)*(-1/sqrt(2))^9=-1/4,0.003*(sqrt(10))^7=3sqrt(10).", "misconception": "Use one extra ratio factor in every term."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Calculate absolute magnitudes but replace (-2)^5 by 2^5, giving positive 4 in B; C's even exponent already gives a positive result, so the other coordinates stay unchanged.", "misconception": "Discard the sign of a negative ratio before exponentiation."},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Using n-2 gives 96/32=3,(1/8)*(-16)=-2,4sqrt(2)*(-1/sqrt(2))^7=-1/2,0.003*(sqrt(10))^5=0.3sqrt(10).", "misconception": "Leave out one adjacent multiplication when counting from the first term."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q04",
      "source_numbers": ["281"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "四个数列分别满足：A：$b_1=3,\\ b_{n+1}=2b_n$；B：$b_1=4,\\ b_{n+1}=-3b_n$；C：$b_1=25,\\ b_{n+1}=5b_n$；D：$b_1=12,\\ b_{n+1}=\\frac12b_n$。按 A、B、C、D 的顺序，哪一组是它们的通项公式？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$(3\\cdot2^n,\\ 4(-3)^n,\\ 25\\cdot5^n,\\ 12(\\frac12)^n)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$(3+2(n-1),\\ 4-3(n-1),\\ 25+5(n-1),\\ 12+\\frac{n-1}{2})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$(3\\cdot2^{n-1},\\ 4(-3)^{n-1},\\ 25\\cdot5^{n-1},\\ 12(\\frac12)^{n-1})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$(3\\cdot2^{n-1},\\ -4\\cdot3^{n-1},\\ 25\\cdot5^{n-1},\\ 12(\\frac12)^{n-1})$", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Convert four recurrences and initial values into complete explicit formulas.",
        "source_solution": "Repeated multiplication from index 1 to n gives b_n=b_1 q^(n-1). The four formulas are 3*2^(n-1), 4*(-3)^(n-1), 25*5^(n-1), 12*(1/2)^(n-1). Each satisfies both b_1 and b_(n+1)=q b_n; the negative multiplier stays inside the power.",
        "unit_reason": "A complete formula tuple makes the initial-condition and recurrence checks apply to all four multiplier types; merely supplying the next term would lose the source task.",
        "concept_blocks": [1],
        "limitations": ["Recognition does not demonstrate independently deriving and writing explicit formulas from recurrences."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["c"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The false rule b_n=b_1q^n gives this tuple. At n=1 its values are 6,-12,125,6 instead of the specified first terms.", "misconception": "Apply a ratio factor already at the first term."},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Replace b_(n+1)=qb_n by b_(n+1)=b_n+q; arithmetic formulas b_1+(n-1)q give the displayed sums, although they do not satisfy the given recurrences.", "misconception": "Convert multiplicative recurrences into additive recurrences."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Each formula has b_1 as its value at n=1 and multiplication by its stated q when n is increased by 1; therefore all four recurrences and initial conditions are met.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Misread (-3)^(n-1) as -3^(n-1), producing -4*3^(n-1) in B. Its first term is -4 and its ratio is positive 3, not the stated first term and multiplier.", "misconception": "Move the negative sign outside a variable power, losing alternating signs."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q05",
      "source_numbers": ["282"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "三个数列分别由 $u_n=2^n$、$v_n=5\\cdot3^n$、$w_n=3\\cdot2^{n+1}$ 给出。哪一组论证能证明这三个数列都是等比数列？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "对任意 $n\\ge1$，$\\frac{u_{n+1}}{u_n}=4$，$\\frac{v_{n+1}}{v_n}=9$，$\\frac{w_{n+1}}{w_n}=4$；各比值不依赖 $n$，故三个数列都是等比数列。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "对任意 $n\\ge1$，$\\frac{u_{n+1}}{u_n}=2$，$\\frac{v_{n+1}}{v_n}=15$，$\\frac{w_{n+1}}{w_n}=6$；各比值不依赖 $n$，故三个数列都是等比数列。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "对任意 $n\\ge1$，$\\frac{u_{n+1}}{u_n}=2$，$\\frac{v_{n+1}}{v_n}=3$，$\\frac{w_{n+1}}{w_n}=2$；各比值不依赖 $n$，故三个数列都是等比数列。", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "对任意 $n\\ge1$，$\\frac{u_{n+1}}{u_n}=\\frac12$，$\\frac{v_{n+1}}{v_n}=\\frac13$，$\\frac{w_{n+1}}{w_n}=\\frac12$；各比值不依赖 $n$，故三个数列都是等比数列。", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Recognize a complete universal adjacent-term quotient proof for each of three exponential sequences.",
        "source_solution": "For every n>=1: (2^(n+1))/(2^n)=2; (5*3^(n+1))/(5*3^n)=3; (3*2^(n+2))/(3*2^(n+1))=2. Each quotient is independent of n, proving the definition, not just a finite sample. First terms are 2,15,12 respectively and the ratios are 2,3,2.",
        "unit_reason": "One full proof tuple preserves all three universal calculations and the inference to the definition. Separate finite-term checks or three yes/no items would not retain the proof task.",
        "concept_blocks": [1],
        "limitations": ["Recognizing a valid universal proof does not demonstrate composing the three proofs unaided."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["c"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The two-step quotients u_(n+2)/u_n,v_(n+2)/v_n,w_(n+2)/w_n are 4,9,4. Substituting these values into adjacent-term quotients gives the false displayed identities.", "misconception": "Use a two-index jump when checking the ratio between adjacent terms."},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "For v, fail to cancel the numerator coefficient 5 against the denominator coefficient 5, yielding 5*3=15; for w similarly leave 3*2=6. u has no outer coefficient and remains 2.", "misconception": "Retain a common outer coefficient instead of cancelling it in the quotient."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "All terms are nonzero. Cancellation gives 2^(n+1-n)=2,3^(n+1-n)=3,2^(n+2-(n+1))=2 for every positive n. These constant adjacent ratios prove all three claims.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Compute backward quotients u_n/u_(n+1),v_n/v_(n+1),w_n/w_(n+1), obtaining 1/2,1/3,1/2, then label them as forward quotients. The assertions as written are false.", "misconception": "Reverse numerator and denominator while keeping the displayed forward-ratio claim."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q06",
      "source_numbers": ["283"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "等比数列 A 中，第 $8$ 项是 $384$，公比是 $2$；等比数列 B 中，第 $6$ 项是 $\\frac{32}{81}$，公比是 $-\\frac23$。按 A、B 的顺序，它们的首项是哪一组？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$(3,\\ 3)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$(3,\\ -3)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$(6,\\ 2)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$(\\frac32,\\ \\frac92)$", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Recover the complete pair of first terms from non-first terms and signed ratios.",
        "source_solution": "a: b_1=384/2^7=384/128=3. b: q^5=(-2/3)^5=-32/243, hence b_1=(32/81)/(-32/243)=(32/81)*(-243/32)=-3. Forward substitution gives 3*128=384 and (-3)*(-32/243)=32/81.",
        "unit_reason": "Both inverse-term calculations share the division-by-power rule but one requires an odd negative power. The pair retains this distinction in one coherent result.",
        "concept_blocks": [1],
        "limitations": ["Selection does not demonstrate independently writing the inverse-power calculations."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["b"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Divide the B endpoint by (2/3)^5 instead of (-2/3)^5: (32/81)/(32/243)=3. A remains 384/128=3.", "misconception": "Drop the sign of the negative ratio when computing its odd power."},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Seven factors of 2 and five factors of -2/3 connect each first term to its endpoint; division gives 3 and -3, and forward multiplication verifies both.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Divide by q^(n-2) instead of q^(n-1): 384/2^6=6 and (32/81)/(-2/3)^4=(32/81)/(16/81)=2.", "misconception": "Remove only n-2 ratio factors instead of the required n-1."},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Divide by q^n: 384/256=3/2 and (32/81)/(64/729)=9/2.", "misconception": "Remove n factors when only n-1 connect the first term to the given term."}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
