        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Apply the first-term formula with a_5 incorrectly treated as a_1: exponents j-1 become 6,15,39.", "misconception": "Ignore the given anchor's index and count transitions from index 1."},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Count both endpoints as ratio steps from 5 to j, using j-5+1; the resulting exponents are 3,12,36.", "misconception": "Count terms in the segment rather than transitions between them."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Use the additive rule a_j=a_5+(j-5)q, yielding the displayed sums instead of products.", "misconception": "Treat a common ratio as an additive increment."},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "The index differences 7-5,16-5,40-5 are 2,11,35, giving the displayed powers of q multiplying a_5.", "misconception": null}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q08",
      "source_numbers": ["285"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "四个等比数列分别满足：A：$b_1=2,b_8=256$；B：$b_1=5,b_9=1280$；C：$b_6=25,b_8=9$；D：$b_4=2,b_7=-54$。按 A、B、C、D 的顺序，哪一组给出了各数列公比的全部实数取值？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$(\\{2\\},\\ \\{2\\},\\ \\{\\frac35\\},\\ \\{-3\\})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$(\\{-2,2\\},\\ \\{-2,2\\},\\ \\{-\\frac35,\\frac35\\},\\ \\{-3,3\\})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$(\\{2\\},\\ \\{-2,2\\},\\ \\{-\\frac9{25},\\frac9{25}\\},\\ \\{-3\\})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$(\\{2\\},\\ \\{-2,2\\},\\ \\{-\\frac35,\\frac35\\},\\ \\{-3\\})$", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Determine the full real-ratio sets across odd and even index gaps.",
        "source_solution": "a: 2q^7=256 => q^7=128=2^7, so the unique real q is 2; an odd power excludes -2. b: 5q^8=1280 => q^8=256=2^8, so q=2 or -2. c: 25q^2=9 => q^2=9/25, so q=3/5 or -3/5. d: 2q^3=-54 => q^3=-27, so the unique real q is -3. Each proposed root satisfies the corresponding power equation; these exhaust the real roots by odd-power injectivity or even-power sign alternatives.",
        "unit_reason": "A complete tuple of solution sets preserves the essential distinction between unique odd-power roots and both even-power signs. A single witness or per-sign click would omit the exhaustive-solution task.",
        "concept_blocks": [1],
        "limitations": ["Recognition does not demonstrate unaided solving of the four power equations or written completeness arguments."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["d"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Take only the principal positive roots of q^8=256 and q^2=9/25, giving 2 and 3/5. The missing -2 and -3/5 satisfy those original equations.", "misconception": "Use the principal root operation as if it enumerated every solution of an even-power equation."},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Attach both signs to every extracted root. But (-2)^7=-128, not 128, and 3^3=27, not -27, so the added odd-power roots fail.", "misconception": "Apply the even-power plus/minus rule also to odd powers."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "From q^2=9/25 remove the exponent without taking a square root, obtaining |q|=9/25 and both signs. Their squares are 81/625, not 9/25.", "misconception": "Treat a square as absolute value and leave the squared magnitude unchanged."},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "The exponent gaps 7,8,2,3 give q^7=128,q^8=256,q^2=9/25,q^3=-27. Their complete real solution sets are exactly those displayed.", "misconception": null}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q09",
      "source_numbers": ["286"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "一个等比数列的第 $8$ 项为 $13$，公比为 $-3$。按第 $10$ 项、第 $13$ 项的顺序，所求结果是哪一组？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$(117,\\ 3159)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$(7,\\ -2)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$(117,\\ -3159)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$(-351,\\ 9477)$", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Find two later terms with even and odd signed-ratio gaps from one anchor.",
        "source_solution": "The tenth term is 13*(-3)^(10-8)=13*9=117. The thirteenth term is 13*(-3)^(13-8)=13*(-243)=-3159. Gaps 2 and 5 have different parity.",
        "unit_reason": "The pair shares a known eighth-term anchor but deliberately contrasts even and odd gaps; splitting would hide that comparison.",
        "concept_blocks": [1],
        "limitations": ["Selection does not demonstrate written evaluation of both anchored powers."],
