        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Find all four positive term indices, including reciprocal and decimal cases.",
        "source_solution": "a: 3^(n-1)=162/2=81=3^4 => n=5. b: (1/2)^(n-1)=10/640=1/64=(1/2)^6 => n=7. c: (1/3)^(n-1)=1/81=(1/3)^4 => n=5. d: (0.1)^(n-1)=0.002/2=0.001=(0.1)^3 => n=4. Each positive base other than 1 gives a unique exponent, and the indices are positive integers.",
        "unit_reason": "The full tuple compares exponent counts with term indices across four ratio representations; it is not split into four isolated numerical blanks.",
        "concept_blocks": [1],
        "limitations": ["Selection does not demonstrate independently solving and writing the four exponential equations."],
