          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Mistakenly use the two given endpoints as a two-step count: q^2=16 gives q=4; the first three generated terms are 4,16,64. Continuing this ratio gives final term 256, not the required 16.", "misconception": "Use the count of given endpoints instead of the four actual adjacent transitions."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "The full sequence 1,2,4,8,16 has constant ratio 2 and exactly the required three inserted terms.", "misconception": null},
