        "source_solution": "a: Five total terms give four gaps; 1*q^4=16 => q=2 or -2. q=2 gives (2,4,8); q=-2 gives (-2,4,-8). Both lead to final term 16, and there are no other real fourth roots. b: Seven total terms give six gaps; 60*q^6=15/16 => q^6=(15/16)/60=1/64 => q=1/2 or -1/2. The positive insertion is (30,15,15/2,15/4,15/8); the negative insertion is (-30,15,-15/2,15/4,-15/8). The seventh term in both cases is 60/64=15/16; the real sixth-root alternatives exhaust the constructions.",
