          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "Keep A correct, but take B's second printed term 640 as its first term. Then 640*(1/2)^(n-1)=20 gives n-1=5 and n=6.", "misconception": "Shift the initial anchor to the second displayed term while retaining the original indexing."}
