    {
      "id": "q18",
      "source_numbers": ["294"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "single",
        "stem": "在原式有定义的条件下，化简下列两个式子：\n\n$A=\\left(-\\frac{16x^{4n+7}}{y^3}\\right)\\div\\left(\\frac{8x^{3n+5}}{y^2}\\right)$；\n\n$B=\\left(\\frac{81a^{4n-1}}{25}\\right)^3\\cdot\\left(\\frac5{27a^{3n-1}}\\right)^4$。\n\n按 A、B 的顺序，哪一组给出与原式相等的化简结果？",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$(-\\frac{2x^{7n+12}}{y},\\ \\frac{a^{24n-7}}{25})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$(-2x^{n+2}y,\\ 25a)$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$(-\\frac{2x^{n+2}}{y},\\ \\frac a{25})$", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$(-\\frac{2x^{n+2}}{y},\\ \\frac1{25a})$", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Simplify both original expressions by valid power laws and coefficient cancellation, only on their original domains; do not enumerate n's range or extend a domain.",
        "source_solution": "On the original-expression-defined domain, a: invert the nonzero divisor to obtain (-16/8)*x^((4n+7)-(3n+5))*y^(2-3)=-2x^(n+2)/y. b: the coefficient is 81^3*5^4/(25^3*27^4)=3^12*5^4/(5^6*3^12)=1/25, and the exponent of a is 3(4n-1)-4(3n-1)=1, so the product is a/25. These are equality identities on the original domains only, not a declaration that all values admitted by the simplified expressions are admitted by the originals.",
        "unit_reason": "The quotient and powered-fraction product share the division-exponent and coefficient-cancellation structure. A full pair preserves both symbolic simplifications, with their original defined-input boundary visible.",
        "concept_blocks": [],
        "limitations": ["Recognition does not demonstrate independently writing all simplification steps.", "The parameter n range is not supplied or determined; no complete explicit domain independent of n is claimed. The original-domain boundary is retained, not broadened."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["c"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "In A add the x exponents despite division: (4n+7)+(3n+5)=7n+12. In B likewise add the numerator and denominator a exponents: 3(4n-1)+4(3n-1)=24n-7. The correct coefficient work does not repair these false quotient laws.", "misconception": "Apply the product law to division of powers, adding exponents instead of subtracting denominator exponents."},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "For A reverse the y exponent subtraction from 2-3 to 3-2, giving a y factor. For B reverse the cancellation of the 5-powers: use 5^(6-4)=25 instead of 5^(4-6)=1/25. The x and a exponents otherwise remain correct.", "misconception": "Reverse numerator and denominator ordering in the y-power and numeric 5-power cancellations."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "A has coefficient -2, x exponent (4n+7)-(3n+5)=n+2 and y exponent -1. B has coefficient 1/25 and a exponent 3(4n-1)-4(3n-1)=1. The source expressions remain the domain authority; the pre-options clarification record checks positive, real-defined negative and any admitted zero-base cases without choosing n's range.", "misconception": null},
