        "source_solution": "For y=3 solve 4x^2-5x+4=0, whose discriminant is 25-4*4*4=-39<0; there is no real x. For y=6 solve 4x^2-5x+1=0=(4x-1)(x-1); the complete real set is {1/4,1}. Substitution gives y(1/4)=1/4-5/4+7=6 and y(1)=4-5+7=6. As an independent existence check, y=4(x-5/8)^2+87/16, whose minimum 87/16 exceeds 3 but is below 6.",
